English：
CC0-A License

This is a variant of Creative Commons Zero (CC0) 1.0 Universal.
The "A" stands for "Attribution Requirement" and "Anti-Abuse" —
closed-source use requires attribution (legally binding), and the
attribution right may not be used to maliciously suppress competition.

This license text itself is released under the CC0 Public Domain Dedication.
See below for the CC0 dedication of this license text.

