--- ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENT (BINDING) ---

If You distribute or make the Work available in a form that is NOT
source-available (i.e., "closed-source" or "proprietary" form, including
but not limited to compiled binaries, executable programs, or any form
where the complete source code is not freely accessible to downstream
users), You must:

  (a) Include prominent attribution in the software documentation, "About"
      screen, README file, or equivalent location, crediting the original
      author(s) and indicating the source of the Work;

  (b) Not remove, obscure, or alter any attribution notices, author names,
      or license identifiers present in the Work;

  (c) Include a copy of this license or a URL to where the license text
      can be found.

Attribution example:
  "Based on [Project Name] by [Author Name]"
  "Source: [URL]"

--- ANTI-ABUSE PROVISION (BINDING) ---

The attribution right and license terms granted under this License may not
be used by any party to:

  (a) Maliciously restrict competition, i.e., to deliberately hinder,
      exclude, or impair the ability of other developers or companies to
      compete in the same or related markets;

  (b) Assert copyright or license claims solely for the purpose of harming
      a competitor's business interests, rather than to protect legitimate
      intellectual property rights;

  (c) Prevent or obstruct other users' lawful use, modification, or
      redistribution of the Work or derivative works under the terms of
      this License.

A party's good-faith enforcement of the attribution requirements in this
License shall not be presumed to violate this Anti-Abuse Provision.

--- LICENSE TEXT DEDICATION (SELF-DEDICATION) ---

This CC0-A license text is hereby dedicated to the Creative Commons Zero (CC0)
1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication by this very license. The person who
associated a Work with this License (the "Affirmer") dedicates this license text
to the Commons by relinquishing all copyright and related rights in this license
